    <string name="guide_title">User guide</string>
    <string name="guide_1_title">1. Connect the housing</string>
    <string name="guide_1_text">Turn on the housing, then on the home screen tap "Scan" or tap your housing directly in the paired devices list.</string>
    <string name="guide_2_title">2. Camera</string>
    <string name="guide_2_text">The camera screen takes photos and videos. The housing buttons control: shutter, focus, zoom, photo/video, flash and menu.</string>
    <string name="guide_3_title">3. Camera settings</string>
    <string name="guide_3_text">The ⚙ button (or the housing "menu" button) opens the settings: white balance, image size, video size and exposure.</string>
    <string name="guide_4_title">4. Diving</string>
    <string name="guide_4_text">As soon as the depth exceeds 1.2 m, a dive starts (timer, max depth). It ends automatically when ascending above 0.5 m and is saved to the logbook.</string>
    <string name="guide_5_title">5. Dive settings</string>
    <string name="guide_5_text">Choose SCUBA or Freedive mode, enable alerts (depth, time, ascent rate, safety stop) and units (meters/feet, °C/°F).</string>
    <string name="guide_6_title">6. Compass</string>
    <string name="guide_6_text">The compass uses the phone sensor to show the heading. Open it via the "Compass" button or the dedicated housing button.</string>

